1. All the methods (move(), special_move(), and use()) have the same purpose of performing an action when called. They have the same method names across different classes but produce different behaviors depending on the object.

2. This activity shows polymorphism because different game characters and items can use the same method name to perform different actions. For example, a Warrior swings a sword while a Mage casts a spell using the same special_move() method.

3. Other examples include an attack action, where a Warrior attacks using a sword, a Mage uses magic, and an Archer shoots an arrow. Another example is an equip action, where different items provide different equipment effects.
